  "worked_solution": "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a single step of a numerical method, when the step begins from an exact value. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+\u0394x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+\u0394y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that the exact solution of the initial value problem is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+1.$ Now, let's find the $y$-increment given by the numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+{y}_{\\text{exact}}(x))\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+{x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+x+1)\\cdot \u0394x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exact value at ${x}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}}) & =({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+\u0394x) \\\\  & =(x+\u0394x)^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2x\\cdot \u0394x+(\u0394x)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the LTE for step $n$ starting at $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot \u0394x+(\u0394x)^{2}+1]-[{x}^{2}+1+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+x+1)\\cdot \u0394x] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{2}+1-1+(2x-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+x+1))\\cdot \u0394x+(\u0394x)^{2} \\\\  & =(2x-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}+x+1))\\cdot \u0394x+(\u0394x)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
